# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
# Anchored: the packaging build directory only. paper/build/ holds the rendered
# manuscript and *is* tracked — tests/test_manuscript_consistency.py compares against it.
/build/
dist/
.eggs/
.venv/
venv/

# Tooling
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Editors / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Model checkpoints are regenerable by train.py and are not tracked; their sha256
# is recorded in results/ instead.
checkpoints/
*.pt
*.pth

# Never in this repository (hard rule): no binaries, no runtimes, no patient data.
*.exe
*.dll
*.dcm
*.ima

# The review PDF is a derivative of build/manuscript.md + results/ + figures/, rebuilt by one
# command (`python paper/build_pdf.py`) and ~1.4 MB per rebuild. The built Markdown is the
# readable record in git; committing a binary on every proof-reading cycle is not. The .docx is
# the same derivative by another renderer (`python paper/build_docx.py`), and stays out for the
# same reason.
paper/build/*.pdf
paper/build/*.docx

# results/ is deliberately NOT ignored: every number in the manuscript is read
# back from it by tests/test_manuscript_consistency.py.

# The internal briefs stay local. They are working documents, they name the commercial scope
# this open core deliberately excludes, and they quote the affiliation policy verbatim —
# including the institution names that must not appear anywhere in the public repository.
*_PROPOSAL.md
paper/cover_letter_medphys.txt
paper/susy_medphys_fields.txt
